examples.question_text:
(a) A square has area $81$ cm$^{2}$. Find its side length.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[black] (0,0) rectangle (3,3);
\path (1.5,1.5) node {$81\,\mathrm{cm}^{2}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(b) A cube has volume $125$ cm$^{3}$. Find its edge length.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
% Closed cube: front z=0, rear z=1; projection (x,y,z) -> (x+0.8z,y+0.6z).
% View towards viewer is proportional to (0.8,0.6,-1); front, top and right faces are visible.
% Faces: front ABCD, rear EFGH, bottom ABFE, right BCGF, top DCGH, left ADHE.
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (3,0);
\coordinate (C) at (3,3);
\coordinate (D) at (0,3);
\coordinate (E) at (0.8,0.6);
\coordinate (F) at (3.8,0.6);
\coordinate (G) at (3.8,3.6);
\coordinate (H) at (0.8,3.6);
\draw[black] (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--cycle;
\draw[black] (D)--(H)--(G)--(C);
\draw[black] (B)--(F)--(G);
\draw[black,dashed] (A)--(E)--(H);
\draw[black,dashed] (E)--(F);
\path (1.5,1.5) node {$125\,\mathrm{cm}^{3}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
(a) The side length is $\sqrt{81}=9$ cm, since $9^{2}=81$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[black] (0,0) rectangle (3,3);
\path (1.5,1.5) node {$81\,\mathrm{cm}^{2}$};
\path (1.5,0) node[below] {$9\,\mathrm{cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(b) The edge length is $\sqrt[3]{125}=5$ cm, since $5^{3}=125$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
% Closed cube: front z=0, rear z=1; projection (x,y,z) -> (x+0.8z,y+0.6z).
% View towards viewer is proportional to (0.8,0.6,-1); front, top and right faces are visible.
% Faces: front ABCD, rear EFGH, bottom ABFE, right BCGF, top DCGH, left ADHE.
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (3,0);
\coordinate (C) at (3,3);
\coordinate (D) at (0,3);
\coordinate (E) at (0.8,0.6);
\coordinate (F) at (3.8,0.6);
\coordinate (G) at (3.8,3.6);
\coordinate (H) at (0.8,3.6);
\draw[black] (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--cycle;
\draw[black] (D)--(H)--(G)--(C);
\draw[black] (B)--(F)--(G);
\draw[black,dashed] (A)--(E)--(H);
\draw[black,dashed] (E)--(F);
\path (1.5,1.5) node {$125\,\mathrm{cm}^{3}$};
\path (1.5,0) node[below] {$5\,\mathrm{cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
